{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Build Sharma Retail's Complete Three-Statement Model & Balance",
  "scenario": "You are a junior analyst at a Mumbai equity desk. Your manager has asked you to build a small, complete three-statement financial model for Sharma Retail Ltd (FY25 actual, FY26 forecast) using given assumptions. The P&L, balance sheet, and cash flow must link correctly — and the balance sheet must balance by construction, not by plugging cash. Your job: build the statements, compute closing cash from the cash flow, link it back, and verify the balance check reads zero.",
  "instructions": "Build a complete three-statement model (P&L, balance sheet, cash flow) for Sharma Retail Ltd using the given FY25 actuals and FY26 assumptions; compute and link closing cash from the cash flow statement into the balance sheet; verify the balance check equals zero by answering the five calculation questions in the Answers sheet.",
  "learning_objective": "Construct a fully integrated three-statement financial model, compute closing cash independently via the cash flow statement, link it back to balance the balance sheet, and verify the model's correctness using a balance check.",
  "hints": [
    "FY26 revenue = FY25 revenue × (1 + growth rate); costs are driven by margins and percentages, not typed as fixed numbers.",
    "Balance sheet: PP&E rolls forward as opening + capex − depreciation; reserves roll forward as opening + PAT − dividends; working capital lines grow with revenue. Cash is left blank on purpose.",
    "Cash flow: CFO = PAT + depreciation − (changes in inventory, receivables) + (change in payables); CFI = −capex; CFF = −dividends. Closing cash = opening cash + CFO + CFI + CFF. This closing cash plugs into the blank balance sheet cash cell via a link formula (=), and the balance check then reads zero."
  ],
